- Article Three (Eligible Employee) gives the Committee sole discretion to designate which Employees may participate and to maintain records of eligibility.
- Even if initially eligible, an Employee becomes ineligible and forfeits all benefits if the Committee (in its sole, final, and binding discretion) determines the Employee:
  - was terminated for cause;
  - violated noncompete, confidentiality, or similar agreements with the Company;
  - solicited or encouraged Company employees to leave;
  - worked for or provided services to a third party (including competitors) that could harm the Company; or
  - filed or threatened legal action against the Company (including patent-related claims) that could harm the Company.
- If the Committee finds a violation of items (b)–(e), the Employee forfeits all future benefits and must promptly repay any benefits already received.
- An Employee eligible for this Plan is not entitled to benefits under the Corning Incorporated Supplemental Pension Plan.
- Article Four (Benefits) begins and Section 4.1 introduces the benefit amount, but the specific terms are not included in the provided excerpt.
